#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186096302 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "660e7de2-aeea-55ad-971b-3c137ccb1521" :knowledge-point/title "Determining a Rate of Change Given a Related Rate and an Explicit Function"}] :question/id #uuid "1e131c11-ded0-52dc-866f-3073eac4565a" :question/math-academy-id "e-10899" :question/problem "Given that $y=x^3+e^x$ for $x=x(t),$ and that $\\dfrac{\\textrm d y}{\\textrm d t}=2$ at the point where $x=1,$ find $\\dfrac{\\textrm d x}{\\textrm d t}.$" :question/worked-solution "Differentiating the given relation with respect to $t$ using implicit differentiation, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y & ={x}^{3}+{e}^{x} \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(y) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({x}^{3}+{e}^{x}) \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t} & =\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}({x}^{3}+{e}^{x}) \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t} & =\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}\\cdot (3{x}^{2}+{e}^{x}).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow we can substitute the given information $\\dfrac{\\textrm d y}{\\textrm d t}=2$ and $x=1,$ and solve for $\\dfrac{\\textrm d x}{\\textrm d t}.$ We get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2 & =\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}\\cdot (3\\cdot {1}^{2}+{e}^{1}) \\\\ 2 & =\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}\\cdot (3+e) \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t} & =\\frac{2}{3+e}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186096303 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "0f2818fc-787e-5b46-8a7a-c5fbea7905a6" :knowledge-point/title "Determining an Angular Rate Given a Related Rate"}] :question/id #uuid "fdf149d5-0139-5291-ab72-c070fb6a4a6e" :question/math-academy-id "e-10901" :question/problem "Given that $r=\\sin\\theta$ for $\\theta = \\theta(t),$ and that $\\dfrac{\\textrm d r}{\\textrm d t}=\\sqrt{2}$ at the point where $\\theta=\\dfrac{\\pi}{4},$ find $\\dfrac{\\textrm d \\theta}{\\textrm d t}.$" :question/worked-solution "Differentiating the given relation with respect to $t$ using implicit differentiation, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r & =\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta  \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(r) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta ) \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}r}{\\text{d}t} & =\\frac{\\text{d}\\theta }{\\text{d}t}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}\\theta }(\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta ) \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}r}{\\text{d}t} & =\\frac{\\text{d}\\theta }{\\text{d}t}\\cdot \\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta .\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow we can substitute the given information $\\dfrac{\\textrm d r}{\\textrm d t}=\\sqrt{2}$ and $\\theta=\\dfrac{\\pi}{4},$ and solve for $\\dfrac{\\textrm d \\theta}{\\textrm d t}.$ We get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}r}{\\text{d}t} & =\\frac{\\text{d}\\theta }{\\text{d}t}\\cdot \\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta  \\\\ \\sqrt{2} & =\\frac{\\text{d}\\theta }{\\text{d}t}\\cdot \\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{4}) \\\\ \\sqrt{2} & =\\frac{\\text{d}\\theta }{\\text{d}t}\\cdot \\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2} \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}\\theta }{\\text{d}t} & =\\sqrt{2}\\cdot \\frac{2}{\\sqrt{2}} \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}\\theta }{\\text{d}t} & =2.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186096304 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "0b47a8b7-722d-564e-8e7a-ad07577d6f6b" :knowledge-point/title "Determining the Rate of Change of an XY-Coordinate"}] :question/id #uuid "1b0131b8-bc82-5547-9b83-95f2b3e53447" :question/math-academy-id "e-10902" :question/problem "A particle $P$ is moving along the curve $y=x+e^x$ such that the $x$-coordinate of $P$ is changing at the rate of $2 \\,\\textrm{cm}/\\textrm{s}.$ Find the rate of change of the $y$-coordinate when $x=5\\,\\textrm{cm}.$" :question/worked-solution "Differentiating the given relation with respect to $t$ using implicit differentiation, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y & =x+{e}^{x} \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(y) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(x+{e}^{x}) \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t} & =\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(x+{e}^{x}) \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t} & =\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}\\cdot (1+{e}^{x}).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we can substitute the given information $\\dfrac{\\textrm d x}{\\textrm d t}=2 \\,\\textrm{cm}/\\textrm{s}$ and $x=5$ and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t} & =2(1+{e}^{5})\\,\\text{cm}/\\text{s}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186339612 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "0f2818fc-787e-5b46-8a7a-c5fbea7905a6" :knowledge-point/title "Determining an Angular Rate Given a Related Rate"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "56b42973-0fe8-58b6-a0d2-f87bbec1125e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "28" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186339614} {:answer/id #uuid "a7371119-d489-5eb2-a7bd-e7770407dcd0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "26" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186339615} {:answer/id #uuid "76919b84-1c89-5413-a8b5-b7465f4b6dc1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "21" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186339616} {:answer/id #uuid "6c3ac0c4-9e87-5aee-bfdc-4133d83a554e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "32" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186339617} {:answer/id #uuid "72e1ecce-730b-5d03-a7fb-25bd400fbae2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "24" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186339618}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "56b42973-0fe8-58b6-a0d2-f87bbec1125e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "28" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186339614} :answer-field/id #uuid "97c3bf96-63b2-5aa8-9683-0fa684cb6e5d" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186339613}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "07059242-b72a-57d2-8e08-c5ac22ad9ca0" :question/math-academy-id "q-115772" :question/problem "Given that $r=\\theta +6\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta $ for $\\theta =\\theta (t),$ and that $\\frac{\\text{d}\\theta }{\\text{d}t}=7$ at the point where $\\theta =\\frac{7\\pi }{6},$ find $\\frac{\\text{d}r}{\\text{d}t}.$" :question/worked-solution "Differentiating the given relation with respect to $t$ using implicit differentiation, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r & =\\theta +6\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta  \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(r) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\theta +6\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta ) \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}r}{\\text{d}t} & =\\frac{\\text{d}\\theta }{\\text{d}t}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}\\theta }(\\theta +6\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta ) \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}r}{\\text{d}t} & =\\frac{\\text{d}\\theta }{\\text{d}t}\\cdot (1-6\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta ).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow we can substitute the given information $\\frac{\\text{d}\\theta }{\\text{d}t}=7$ and $\\theta =\\frac{7\\pi }{6},$ and solve for $\\frac{\\text{d}r}{\\text{d}t}.$ We get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}r}{\\text{d}t} & =\\frac{\\text{d}\\theta }{\\text{d}t}\\cdot (1-6\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta ) \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}r}{\\text{d}t} & =7\\cdot (1-6\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{7\\pi }{6})) \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}r}{\\text{d}t} & =7\\cdot 4 \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}r}{\\text{d}t} & =28.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186339619 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "0b47a8b7-722d-564e-8e7a-ad07577d6f6b" :knowledge-point/title "Determining the Rate of Change of an XY-Coordinate"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "c2119d83-541a-5f16-ae1e-2f38538ce58a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-33\\,\\text{cm}/\\text{s}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186339621} {:answer/id #uuid "dbe5cc47-b230-5df6-95c8-6891c755c1dc" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-36\\,\\text{cm}/\\text{s}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186339622} {:answer/id #uuid "e3ec4cef-b55d-5d61-bb3d-5b7f82271c1c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-12\\,\\text{cm}/\\text{s}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186339623} {:answer/id #uuid "1992e8f0-106c-5bd5-9914-b069c6483c59" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-31\\,\\text{cm}/\\text{s}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186339624} {:answer/id #uuid "053998b1-258e-5c72-b962-ff5bd0686a3a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-30\\,\\text{cm}/\\text{s}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186339625}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "1992e8f0-106c-5bd5-9914-b069c6483c59" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-31\\,\\text{cm}/\\text{s}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186339624} :answer-field/id #uuid "bd883779-7539-5c1f-9efe-6d9aecbb2766" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186339620}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "50fb4f97-5980-53b3-b2fc-bf511f707ff7" :question/math-academy-id "q-115785" :question/problem "A particle $P$ is moving along the curve $y=4{x}^{3}+16x$ such that the $x$-coordinate of $P$ is changing at the rate of $-\\frac{1}{4}\\,\\text{cm}/\\text{s}.$ Find the rate of change of the $y$-coordinate when $x=3\\,\\text{cm}.$" :question/worked-solution "Differentiating the given relation with respect to $t$ using implicit differentiation, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y & =4{x}^{3}+16x \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(y) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(4{x}^{3}+16x) \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t} & =\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(4{x}^{3}+16x) \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t} & =\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}\\cdot (12{x}^{2}+16).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we can substitute the given information $\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}=-\\frac{1}{4}\\,\\text{cm}/\\text{s}$ and $x=3$ and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t} & =(-\\frac{1}{4})\\cdot (12\\cdot (3)^{2}+16)\\,\\text{cm}/\\text{s} \\\\  & =-31\\,\\text{cm}/\\text{s}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186339626 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "0f2818fc-787e-5b46-8a7a-c5fbea7905a6" :knowledge-point/title "Determining an Angular Rate Given a Related Rate"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "41ec6b23-5b91-5145-83e4-a2817d50c2c8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-10" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186339628}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "41ec6b23-5b91-5145-83e4-a2817d50c2c8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-10" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186339628} :answer-field/id #uuid "b94ebd69-7893-5c7e-8d1e-56ec03b81f89" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186339627}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045464 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "ab4ba7d5-a8ac-5c4e-b369-4be7306d4fc5" :question/math-academy-id "q-313637" :question/problem "Given that $r=5\\operatorname{sec}⁡\\theta $ for $\\theta =\\theta (t),$ and that $\\frac{\\text{d}\\theta }{\\text{d}t}=-3$ at the point where $\\theta =\\frac{\\pi }{6},$ evaluate $\\frac{\\text{d}r}{\\text{d}t}$ at that point.\n\n$\\frac{\\text{d}r}{\\text{d}t}=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "Differentiating the given relation with respect to $t$ using implicit differentiation, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r & =5\\operatorname{sec}⁡\\theta  \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(r) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(5\\operatorname{sec}⁡\\theta ) \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}r}{\\text{d}t} & =\\frac{\\text{d}\\theta }{\\text{d}t}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}\\theta }(5\\operatorname{sec}⁡\\theta ) \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}r}{\\text{d}t} & =\\frac{\\text{d}\\theta }{\\text{d}t}\\cdot (5\\operatorname{sec}⁡\\theta \\operatorname{tan}⁡\\theta ).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow we can substitute the given information $\\frac{\\text{d}\\theta }{\\text{d}t}=-3$ and $\\theta =\\frac{\\pi }{6},$ and solve for $\\frac{\\text{d}r}{\\text{d}t}.$ We get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}r}{\\text{d}t} & =\\frac{\\text{d}\\theta }{\\text{d}t}\\cdot (5\\operatorname{sec}⁡\\theta \\operatorname{tan}⁡\\theta ) \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}r}{\\text{d}t} & =(-3)\\cdot (5\\operatorname{sec}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{6})\\operatorname{tan}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{6})) \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}r}{\\text{d}t} & =(-3)\\cdot 5\\cdot (\\frac{2}{\\sqrt{3}}\\cdot \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{3}}) \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}r}{\\text{d}t} & =-10.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186339629 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "660e7de2-aeea-55ad-971b-3c137ccb1521" :knowledge-point/title "Determining a Rate of Change Given a Related Rate and an Explicit Function"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a6f8f08b-1209-5799-9f8e-3bea955840e8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186339631}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "a6f8f08b-1209-5799-9f8e-3bea955840e8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186339631} :answer-field/id #uuid "3a343f2e-3bce-59c0-8da8-32eb86e84161" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186339630}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "65954d52-ea96-5390-9cfa-b0aa0d4101ec" :question/math-academy-id "q-313855" :question/problem "Given that $y=-{x}^{3}+4{x}^{2}-5x$ for $x=x(t),$ and that $\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}=-3$ at the point where $x=2,$ evaluate $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t}$ at that point.\n\n$\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t}=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "Differentiating the given relation with respect to $t$ using implicit differentiation, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y & =-{x}^{3}+4{x}^{2}-5x \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(y) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(-{x}^{3}+4{x}^{2}-5x) \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t} & =\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(-{x}^{3}+4{x}^{2}-5x) \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t} & =\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}\\cdot (-3{x}^{2}+8x-5).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow we can substitute the given information $\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}=-3$ and $x=2,$ and solve for $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t}.$ We get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t} & =(-3)\\cdot (-3\\cdot (2)^{2}+8\\cdot (2)-5)=3.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186339632 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "660e7de2-aeea-55ad-971b-3c137ccb1521" :knowledge-point/title "Determining a Rate of Change Given a Related Rate and an Explicit Function"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2caa8211-aa10-5c2c-ac0f-b503fca330b1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186339634}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "2caa8211-aa10-5c2c-ac0f-b503fca330b1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186339634} :answer-field/id #uuid "d5200f13-2722-519d-9cb5-2c9037f741b2" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186339633}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "04ce6cd4-ddeb-529d-8ad4-fa72c75dbef3" :question/math-academy-id "q-342697" :question/problem "Given that $y={x}^{2}+1$ for $x=x(t),$ and that $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t}=\\frac{1}{2}$ at the point where $x=1,$ evaluate $\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}$ at that point.\n\n$\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "Differentiating the given relation with respect to $t$ using implicit differentiation, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y & ={x}^{2}+1 \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(y) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({x}^{2}+1) \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t} & =\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}({x}^{2}+1) \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t} & =\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}\\cdot 2x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow we can substitute the given information $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t}=\\frac{1}{2}$ and $x=1,$ and solve for $\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}.$ We get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{2} & =\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}\\cdot 2(1) \\\\ \\frac{1}{2} & =\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}\\,\\cdot 2 \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t} & =\\frac{1}{4}\\,.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186339635 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "0f2818fc-787e-5b46-8a7a-c5fbea7905a6" :knowledge-point/title "Determining an Angular Rate Given a Related Rate"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "f34f2e68-cc30-5ff0-ba8e-4fdbcfcba323" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{6}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186339637}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "f34f2e68-cc30-5ff0-ba8e-4fdbcfcba323" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{6}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186339637} :answer-field/id #uuid "3e23473b-40c0-5f4a-acb0-ed41789a883d" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186339636}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "64ac928e-3cbc-5fc3-997c-9cc3278a4024" :question/math-academy-id "q-342707" :question/problem "Given that $r=-4\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta $ for $\\theta =\\theta (t),$ and that $\\frac{\\text{d}r}{\\text{d}t}=\\frac{1}{3}$ at the point where $\\theta =\\frac{\\pi }{3},$ evaluate $\\frac{\\text{d}\\theta }{\\text{d}t}$ at that point.\n\n$\\frac{\\text{d}\\theta }{\\text{d}t}=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "Differentiating the given relation with respect to $t$ using implicit differentiation, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r & =-4\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta  \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(r) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}\\,(-4\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta ) \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}r}{\\text{d}t} & =\\frac{\\text{d}\\theta }{\\text{d}t}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}\\theta }\\,(-4\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta ) \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}r}{\\text{d}t} & =\\frac{\\text{d}\\theta }{\\text{d}t}\\cdot (-4\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta ).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow we can substitute the given information $\\frac{\\text{d}r}{\\text{d}t}=\\frac{1}{3}$ and $\\theta =\\frac{\\pi }{3},$ and solve for $\\frac{\\text{d}\\theta }{\\text{d}t}.$ We get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{3} & =\\frac{\\text{d}\\theta }{\\text{d}t}\\cdot [-4\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{3})] \\\\ \\frac{1}{3} & =\\frac{\\text{d}\\theta }{\\text{d}t}\\cdot (-2) \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}\\theta }{\\text{d}t} & =-\\frac{1}{6}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186339638 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "0b47a8b7-722d-564e-8e7a-ad07577d6f6b" :knowledge-point/title "Determining the Rate of Change of an XY-Coordinate"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "6c8d67a6-cef9-5d47-98bb-461df3bba6e3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186339640}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "6c8d67a6-cef9-5d47-98bb-461df3bba6e3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186339640} :answer-field/id #uuid "deeb1edc-4564-5578-bed7-e9fbbfd77deb" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186339639}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "a6f176b5-889a-5c1a-aa75-6203cb1a3c50" :question/math-academy-id "q-342736" :question/problem "A particle $P$ is moving along the curve $y=\\sqrt{x+1}$ such that the $x$-coordinate of $P$ is changing at the rate of $-4\\,\\text{cm}/\\text{s}.$ Find the rate of change of the $y$-coordinate when $x=3\\,\\,\\text{cm}.$\n\nThe $y$-coordinate is changing at the rate of \n{{field-1}}\n$\\text{cm}/\\text{s}.$" :question/worked-solution "Differentiating the given relation with respect to $t$ using implicit differentiation, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y & =\\sqrt{x+1} \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(y) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\sqrt{x+1}) \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t} & =\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\sqrt{x+1}) \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t} & =\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}\\cdot \\frac{1}{2\\sqrt{x+1}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we can substitute the given information $\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}=-4\\,\\text{cm}/\\text{s}$ and $x=3$ and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t} & =-4\\cdot \\frac{1}{2\\sqrt{3+1}} \\\\  & =-4\\cdot \\frac{1}{4} \\\\  & =-1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the $y$-coordinate is changing at the rate of $-1\\text{ }\\text{cm}/\\text{s}.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186339641 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "0b47a8b7-722d-564e-8e7a-ad07577d6f6b" :knowledge-point/title "Determining the Rate of Change of an XY-Coordinate"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "88249f5d-1501-5c65-bc86-b1554d487123" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-25" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186339643}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "88249f5d-1501-5c65-bc86-b1554d487123" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-25" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186339643} :answer-field/id #uuid "5d65adfe-9a18-55f9-8b16-3b13e206af06" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186339642}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "37812340-9e80-5efe-8a6b-2a539b36a5af" :question/math-academy-id "q-342740" :question/problem "A particle $P$ is moving along the curve $y=\\operatorname{ln}⁡(x+1)+{x}^{2}$ such that the $x$-coordinate of $P$ is changing at the rate of $-4\\,\\text{cm}/\\text{s}.$ Find the rate of change of the $y$-coordinate when $x=3\\,\\,\\text{cm}.$\n\nThe $y$-coordinate is changing at the rate of \n{{field-1}}\n$\\text{cm}/\\text{s}.$" :question/worked-solution "Differentiating the given relation with respect to $t$ using implicit differentiation, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡(x+1)+{x}^{2} \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(y) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}[\\operatorname{ln}⁡(x+1)+{x}^{2}] \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t} & =\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}[\\operatorname{ln}⁡(x+1)+{x}^{2}] \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t} & =\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}\\cdot (\\frac{1}{x+1}+2x).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we can substitute the given information $\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}=-4\\,\\text{cm}/\\text{s}$ and $x=3$ and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t} & =-4\\cdot (\\frac{1}{3+1}+2(3)) \\\\  & =-4\\cdot (\\frac{1}{4}+6) \\\\  & =-4\\cdot \\frac{25}{4} \\\\  & =-25.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the $y$-coordinate is changing at the rate of $-25\\text{ }\\text{cm}/\\text{s}.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186339644 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "660e7de2-aeea-55ad-971b-3c137ccb1521" :knowledge-point/title "Determining a Rate of Change Given a Related Rate and an Explicit Function"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "8d2fd07d-09a0-5b06-abdd-1ac91212267b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "9" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186339646} {:answer/id #uuid "e28903c7-2b4d-5d8b-b073-a1759a196cdf" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186339647} {:answer/id #uuid "3c032e1a-8171-5c9a-a00c-037b02a4d789" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "8" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186339648} {:answer/id #uuid "219640de-61f8-5c51-9d90-ae8347329ca4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186339649} {:answer/id #uuid "bf8efaad-ff7f-557a-82ec-b59320329551" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186339650}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "219640de-61f8-5c51-9d90-ae8347329ca4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186339649} :answer-field/id #uuid "386fd468-c359-5029-adf3-c864b1246a39" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186339645}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "99ded3a6-6a92-5942-b8b9-2758a74bf429" :question/math-academy-id "q-48763" :question/problem "Given that $y=3x-1$ for $x=x(t),$ and that $\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}=2$ at the point where $x=-1,$ find $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t}.$" :question/worked-solution "Differentiating the given relation with respect to $t$ using implicit differentiation, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y & =3x-1 \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(y) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(3x-1) \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t} & =\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(3x-1) \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t} & =\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}\\cdot (3).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow we can substitute the given information $\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}=2$ and $x=-1,$ and solve for $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t}.$ We get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t} & =2\\cdot (3)=6.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186097172 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "660e7de2-aeea-55ad-971b-3c137ccb1521" :knowledge-point/title "Determining a Rate of Change Given a Related Rate and an Explicit Function"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "82af1229-8171-53dc-abcf-4165fa77d4c4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "22" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186095390} {:answer/id #uuid "9142e4ee-002c-5474-b2ad-6a49ebe6e83f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "24" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186095391} {:answer/id #uuid "c9e19d83-a825-5642-8fb3-bcf22b57de41" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "10" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186095392} {:answer/id #uuid "2251d5a1-9b92-54be-a4e6-0fcb0d019f33" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "28" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186095393} {:answer/id #uuid "27990112-1922-59d6-b566-f6926b995a6f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186095394}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "82af1229-8171-53dc-abcf-4165fa77d4c4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "22" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186095390} :answer-field/id #uuid "8c1a3cef-0549-5117-8a5a-ea6aa5fc7cbd" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186095389}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "123374e6-ecc1-51ff-9e7a-07d1d48a742d" :question/math-academy-id "q-48765" :question/problem "Given that $y=2{x}^{3}-2x$ for $x=x(t),$ and that $\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}=1$ at the point where $x=-2,$ find $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t}.$" :question/requires-calculator true :question/worked-solution "Differentiating the given relation with respect to $t$ using implicit differentiation, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y & =2{x}^{3}-2x \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(y) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(2{x}^{3}-2x) \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t} & =\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(2{x}^{3}-2x) \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t} & =\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}\\cdot (6{x}^{2}-2).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow we can substitute the given information $\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}=1$ and $x=-2,$ and solve for $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t}.$ We get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t} & =1\\cdot (6\\cdot (-2)^{2}-2)=22.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186339651 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "660e7de2-aeea-55ad-971b-3c137ccb1521" :knowledge-point/title "Determining a Rate of Change Given a Related Rate and an Explicit Function"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "c55a9e1f-26d9-5d8e-8739-f4dd43517b1c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186339653} {:answer/id #uuid "67235440-2ef6-502e-925f-fc1765bd7190" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186339654} {:answer/id #uuid "36c304d3-7506-5de2-9e0c-9375f344b29e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186339655} {:answer/id #uuid "bcbedfc5-c2f4-5a20-8604-24e29a3db98d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186339656} {:answer/id #uuid "d066b761-6e5a-5c4d-824b-2ce26ae4c025" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186339657}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "c55a9e1f-26d9-5d8e-8739-f4dd43517b1c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186339653} :answer-field/id #uuid "f7b0147d-7e62-50a3-9fe6-3ae59372a583" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186339652}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "370da794-2fe1-5503-abab-e6edee8fbed0" :question/math-academy-id "q-48770" :question/problem "Given that $y=3{x}^{4}+2{x}^{3}$ for $x=x(t),$ and that $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t}=3$ at the point where $x=-1,$ find $\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}.$" :question/worked-solution "Differentiating the given relation with respect to $t$ using implicit differentiation, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y & =3{x}^{4}+2{x}^{3} \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(y) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(3{x}^{4}+2{x}^{3}) \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t} & =\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(3{x}^{4}+2{x}^{3}) \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t} & =\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}\\cdot (12{x}^{3}+6{x}^{2}).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow we can substitute the given information $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t}=3$ and $x=-1,$ and solve for $\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}.$ We get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3 & =\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}\\cdot (12(-1)^{3}+6(-1)^{2}) \\\\ 3 & =\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}\\cdot (-6) \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t} & =-\\frac{1}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186339658 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "0f2818fc-787e-5b46-8a7a-c5fbea7905a6" :knowledge-point/title "Determining an Angular Rate Given a Related Rate"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "7011cdc9-c928-50da-a7d3-37837e18594c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186339660} {:answer/id #uuid "5d931791-f111-5ed7-a6fd-cd99c0140829" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{3}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186339661} {:answer/id #uuid "e395562f-c6d2-5457-81a9-0d4a92b793c5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186339662} {:answer/id #uuid "f2419fee-a1bb-5863-8bcb-37159e5f55e7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186339663} {:answer/id #uuid "467ac5c5-9524-5a04-b66d-a0d45eac05db" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186339664}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "7011cdc9-c928-50da-a7d3-37837e18594c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186339660} :answer-field/id #uuid "a86d8903-3244-5b9d-8be3-2d32d72dc3be" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186339659}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "55e8556a-5ae1-5690-852b-2dad76c68111" :question/math-academy-id "q-48801" :question/problem "Given that $r=\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta -2$ for $\\theta =\\theta (t),$ and that $\\frac{\\text{d}\\theta }{\\text{d}t}=-3$ at the point where $\\theta =\\pi ,$ find $\\frac{\\text{d}r}{\\text{d}t}.$" :question/worked-solution "Differentiating the given relation with respect to $t$ using implicit differentiation, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r & =\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta -2 \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(r) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta -2) \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}r}{\\text{d}t} & =\\frac{\\text{d}\\theta }{\\text{d}t}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}\\theta }(\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta -2) \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}r}{\\text{d}t} & =\\frac{\\text{d}\\theta }{\\text{d}t}\\cdot (\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta ).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow we can substitute the given information $\\frac{\\text{d}\\theta }{\\text{d}t}=-3$ and $\\theta =\\pi ,$ and solve for $\\frac{\\text{d}r}{\\text{d}t}.$ We get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}r}{\\text{d}t} & =\\frac{\\text{d}\\theta }{\\text{d}t}\\cdot (\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta ) \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}r}{\\text{d}t} & =(-3)\\cdot (\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\pi ) \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}r}{\\text{d}t} & =(-3)\\cdot (-1) \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}r}{\\text{d}t} & =3.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186097175 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "0f2818fc-787e-5b46-8a7a-c5fbea7905a6" :knowledge-point/title "Determining an Angular Rate Given a Related Rate"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a75c02bc-adc8-5003-b427-7b5c1521abb3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186095408} {:answer/id #uuid "ae751400-4a7b-5218-93d5-fefd562175f0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\sqrt{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186095409} {:answer/id #uuid "c023b6d8-a5a8-53a7-87a5-b2c274159bbd" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186095410} {:answer/id #uuid "3fbbbe17-86a4-5c10-8f88-cd816fe1ab5b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186095411} {:answer/id #uuid "7dcb5ab3-421c-5703-88a2-4df7c7550815" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186095412}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "a75c02bc-adc8-5003-b427-7b5c1521abb3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186095408} :answer-field/id #uuid "c5753917-2a28-59b2-b50e-0f0413227d87" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186095407}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "e52c46bb-53c6-584c-86da-75775eac460d" :question/math-academy-id "q-48806" :question/problem "Given that $r=\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta $ for $\\theta =\\theta (t),$ and that $\\frac{\\text{d}r}{\\text{d}t}=\\sqrt{2}$ at the point where $\\theta =\\frac{\\pi }{4},$ find $\\frac{\\text{d}\\theta }{\\text{d}t}.$" :question/worked-solution "Differentiating the given relation with respect to $t$ using implicit differentiation, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r & =\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta  \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(r) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta ) \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}r}{\\text{d}t} & =\\frac{\\text{d}\\theta }{\\text{d}t}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}\\theta }(\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta ) \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}r}{\\text{d}t} & =\\frac{\\text{d}\\theta }{\\text{d}t}\\cdot (-\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta ).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow we can substitute the given information $\\frac{\\text{d}r}{\\text{d}t}=\\sqrt{2}$ and $\\theta =\\frac{\\pi }{4},$ and solve for $\\frac{\\text{d}\\theta }{\\text{d}t}.$ We get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}r}{\\text{d}t} & =\\frac{\\text{d}\\theta }{\\text{d}t}\\cdot \\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta  \\\\ \\sqrt{2} & =\\frac{\\text{d}\\theta }{\\text{d}t}\\cdot (-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{4})) \\\\ \\sqrt{2} & =\\frac{\\text{d}\\theta }{\\text{d}t}\\cdot (-\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}) \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}\\theta }{\\text{d}t} & =-\\sqrt{2}\\cdot \\frac{2}{\\sqrt{2}} \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}\\theta }{\\text{d}t} & =-2.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186339665 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "0b47a8b7-722d-564e-8e7a-ad07577d6f6b" :knowledge-point/title "Determining the Rate of Change of an XY-Coordinate"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0d6bfeeb-66e6-568c-9dd3-00acbe026181" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2(2-8{e}^{2})\\,\\text{cm}/\\text{s}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186339667} {:answer/id #uuid "79ccbd2b-aeb6-5da3-89a2-840bd87940aa" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2(8-3{e}^{2})\\,\\text{cm}/\\text{s}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186339668} {:answer/id #uuid "614d5477-6d94-5213-8e45-0b4d7808110d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(8+2{e}^{2})\\,\\text{cm}/\\text{s}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186339669} {:answer/id #uuid "e6271ea2-d733-5c9f-a29f-c8d91b5ab3dc" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2(2+{e}^{2})\\,\\text{cm}/\\text{s}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186339670} {:answer/id #uuid "046e9722-05a5-5b19-b50f-f029cb92380d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "8-{e}^{2}\\,\\text{cm}/\\text{s}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186339671}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "79ccbd2b-aeb6-5da3-89a2-840bd87940aa" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2(8-3{e}^{2})\\,\\text{cm}/\\text{s}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186339668} :answer-field/id #uuid "44772783-fc80-5623-8ee8-fc21629f8da8" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186339666}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "47f60e14-5051-5f60-9121-3f253fa28394" :question/math-academy-id "q-72227" :question/problem "A particle $P$ is moving along the curve $y=2{x}^{2}-3{e}^{x}$ such that the $x$-coordinate of $P$ is changing at the rate of $2\\,\\text{cm}/\\text{s}.$ Find the rate of change of the $y$-coordinate when $x=2\\,\\text{cm}.$" :question/worked-solution "Differentiating the given relation with respect to $t$ using implicit differentiation, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y & =2{x}^{2}-3{e}^{x} \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(y) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(2{x}^{2}-3{e}^{x}) \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t} & =\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(2{x}^{2}-3{e}^{x}) \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t} & =\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}\\cdot (4x-3{e}^{x}).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we can substitute the given information $\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}=2\\,\\text{cm}/\\text{s}$ and $x=2$ and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t} & =2(4\\cdot (2)-3{e}^{2})\\,\\text{cm}/\\text{s} \\\\  & =2(8-3{e}^{2})\\,\\text{cm}/\\text{s}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186339672 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "0b47a8b7-722d-564e-8e7a-ad07577d6f6b" :knowledge-point/title "Determining the Rate of Change of an XY-Coordinate"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "697d8dc2-dd01-5e8e-ac51-f18c30047e28" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-4\\,\\text{cm}/\\text{s}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186339674} {:answer/id #uuid "b29dd502-29c0-5dc2-9d60-36afc147b0b9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "7\\,\\text{cm}/\\text{s}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186339675} {:answer/id #uuid "9034652d-b7d0-5d39-8d82-e14842be3042" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "9\\,\\text{cm}/\\text{s}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186339676} {:answer/id #uuid "614e3443-28d3-545a-bf14-0c76137e518f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6\\,\\text{cm}/\\text{s}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186339677} {:answer/id #uuid "4463c5e5-4cb5-5c85-ab4e-d3f05ebc4c39" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-6\\,\\text{cm}/\\text{s}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186339678}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "4463c5e5-4cb5-5c85-ab4e-d3f05ebc4c39" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-6\\,\\text{cm}/\\text{s}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186339678} :answer-field/id #uuid "69838466-cfc7-5768-ad39-5166a99a0b67" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186339673}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "a4c40fff-4d18-5542-8848-571c276df41d" :question/math-academy-id "q-72231" :question/problem "A particle $P$ is moving along the curve $y={x}^{2}-6x$ such that the $x$-coordinate of $P$ is changing at the rate of $3\\,\\text{cm}/\\text{s}.$ Find the rate of change of the $y$-coordinate when $x=2\\,\\text{cm}.$" :question/worked-solution "Differentiating the given relation with respect to $t$ using implicit differentiation, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y & ={x}^{2}-6x \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(y) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({x}^{2}-6x) \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t} & =\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}({x}^{2}-6x) \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t} & =\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}\\cdot (2x-6).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we can substitute the given information $\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}=3\\,\\text{cm}/\\text{s}$ and $x=2$ and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t} & =3\\cdot (2\\cdot 2-6)\\,\\text{cm}/\\text{s} \\\\  & =-6\\,\\text{cm}/\\text{s}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}]}
